# Code Review

## Directives

{{#workflow}}
- Read `{{workflow-file}}` to identify the current issue and review scope
- Update `{{workflow-file}}` to `phase: review` when changing phase, then send its complete content using `send_file_content`
{{/workflow}}

- Obtain two fresh, independent reviews of the selected target, using the heavier available model at medium or high effort for one review and a different lighter available model at its highest supported effort for the other
- Run those reviews concurrently in isolated subprocesses when separate subprocess execution is supported; otherwise run them sequentially without exposing either reviewer to the other's findings
- Give each reviewer only the selected target, the relevant repository evidence, governing repository guidance, applicable OpenSpec artefacts, and the required report format
- Do not provide, load, or ask either reviewer to account for prior conversation, prior reviews, existing review records, collated inventories, or findings from another source
- Require both reviews to inspect the selected diff and surrounding code, governing repository guidance, and applicable OpenSpec artefacts; each review must return prioritised P1-to-P6 findings with location, analysis, and recommendation
- Use the workflow file's required `issue` field as the review key. If it is empty, report that there is no active workflow issue and do not dispatch reviewers
- Require every reviewer to write only its own fresh JSON report to `{{path.documents}}Reviews/<issue>/<agent-name>.json`, using a unique lowercase hyphenated agent name such as `codex-heavy` or `codex-light`; do not load, merge, or update adjacent review records while writing it
- Before dispatch, determine the next positive review version for each reviewer without exposing its earlier findings. Pass that version to the reviewer, which overwrites its own report and assigns the same `version` to every finding in that report
- Each source report must identify its reviewer, version, target, scope, and creation time, and contain a `findings` array whose entries have a stable identifier, version, P1-to-P6 priority, location, description, analysis, and recommendation
- After both fresh reviews are complete, collate only the two reports produced for this review: deduplicate the same underlying defect, retain the strongest evidence, and write the canonical combined inventory to `{{path.documents}}Reviews/<issue>.json`
- For a pull-request target, inspect existing pull-request comments only after the fresh reviews are complete. Mark a matching combined finding as already flagged or add useful context there; do not expose those comments to reviewers or alter their source reports
- Preserve source reports as independent evidence. Record all user decisions, variations, actions, and completion state only in the corresponding finding of the combined inventory
- Use `guide://$just-one` when the user explicitly elects it, or when their established preference is to triage findings sequentially; otherwise use the user's requested presentation or ordinary review presentation
- Keep handoff context `{{path.documents}}context.json` updated at meaningful milestones when present

## Source review record format

```json
{
  "reviewer": "<model used>",
  "version": 1,
  "target": "<selected review target>",
  "scope": "<review scope>",
  "created_at": "<ISO 8601 timestamp>",
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "<agent-#>",
      "version": 1,
      "priority": "P#",
      "location": {"file": "<path>", "start": 1, "end": 1},
      "description": "<short description>",
      "analysis": "<evidence and consequence>",
      "recommendation": "<specific action>"
    }
  ]
}
```

## Combined inventory format

```json
{
  "issue": "<workflow issue>",
  "target": "<selected review target>",
  "created_at": "<ISO 8601 timestamp>",
  "source_reports": [
    {"reviewer": "<agent-name>", "version": 1, "path": "Reviews/<issue>/<agent-name>.json"}
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "<combined-#>",
      "sources": [{"reviewer": "<agent-name>", "id": "<agent-#>", "version": 1}],
      "priority": "P#",
      "location": {"file": "<path>", "start": 1, "end": 1},
      "description": "<short description>",
      "analysis": "<evidence and consequence>",
      "recommendation": "<specific action>",
      "triage": {
        "decision": "pending",
        "variation": null,
        "rationale": null,
        "action": null,
        "completion": "not started"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Modes: what to review
{{#kwargs.mode}}- Use `{{kwargs.mode}}` as the review target
{{/kwargs.mode}}{{^kwargs.mode}}- The server may request `review-target` before this skill is rendered. If it does not, ask the user to choose a target using the client's choice-picker interaction
  - Uncommitted work — review the complete working tree against `HEAD`
  - Current change — review the current change against `main`
  - Named branch — review that branch against its merge base
  - Pull request — review a pull-request URL, `<owner>/<repo>/pulls/#<number>` reference, or current-repository pull-request number
  - When the client cannot render a choice picker, present these same options as a numbered list and ask the user to select one
  - Do not begin the review until the user selects a target
{{/kwargs.mode}}
- `mode=uncommitted` — the complete working tree against `HEAD`
- `mode=main` — the current change against `main`
- A branch name — that branch's change against its merge base
- A pull-request URL, `<owner>/<repo>/pulls/#<number>` reference, or current-repository pull-request number — that pull request
- A numeric value — that pull-request number in the current repository
- An unsupported mode — ask the user to clarify; do not infer another review scope

## Guidelines

- Read `guide://review/general` for requirements on reviewing the code

{{#openspec}}
## OpenSpec Association

- Run `openspec validate <active-change> --strict` before completing the review, using the active change identified by the workflow or the reviewed work
- Compare implementation against the active change's proposal, design, specifications, and tasks
{{/openspec}}

## Guardrails

- Keep both reviews independent; do not provide prior findings, conclusions, prior conversation, existing review records, or one reviewer's output to the other
- Do not implement, format, commit, push, or discard changes during review or finding triage unless the user explicitly confirms the collected accepted actions
